2026-09-27T10:26:24.9252678Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9252907Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9253230Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9253545Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9253712Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9253898Z ================
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9253989Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9254118Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9254405Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9254791Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9254890Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9255109Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9255249Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9255360Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9255642Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9255909Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9256406Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9256792Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9256883Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9257223Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9257642Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9257851Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9258072Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9258362Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9258431Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9258591Z ========
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9258683Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9259596Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9260539Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9260732Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9261091Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9319262Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9320106Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9320790Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9321289Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9321744Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9321853Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9322136Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9322298Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9323536Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9325160Z 
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9325966Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9327066Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:26:24.9327359Z 
